    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">After the inspection, the delivery agent will share the findings with the customer and provide a detailed report on any observed damages, issues, or changes.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>To ensure accuracy and transparency in the vehicle's mileage, the following steps will be followed:</p>

	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Verification Against LR Bill of Lading:</strong> The delivery agent will cross-check the vehicle's odometer reading against the details provided in the LR (Loading Receipt) Bill of Lading.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Compare with Previous Mileage:</strong> If available, the delivery agent will also compare the current mileage with the previous reading documented at the pickup point.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Notify Customer of Odometer Verification:</strong> After verifying the odometer reading, the delivery agent will inform the customer and provide a report detailing the mileage verification process.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<p>Upon completing the above inspections, the delivery agent will ensure a signed condition sign-off from the customer acknowledging the vehicle's current condition:</p>

	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Customer Signature:</strong> The delivery agent will obtain a signed copy of the condition report document, indicating the customer's agreement with the findings and acknowledging the vehicle's current condition.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Mileage Verification:</strong> The signed document will also include the verified odometer reading, ensuring transparency and accountability.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Vehicle Inspection Report:</strong> The signed document will provide a detailed account of the vehicle's condition, including any damages, scratches, or other issues observed during the inspection process.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<p>By having the customer sign off on the condition report, both parties will have a documented record of the vehicle's current state, ensuring mutual understanding and reducing the chances of any disputes or discrepancies.</p>

	<p>It is important to conduct these procedures during daylight hours for optimal visibility and safety. Following these steps will ensure a thorough and accurate assessment of the vehicle's condition upon delivery, ensuring customer satisfaction and maintaining trust between the involved parties.</p>

	<p>Upon completion of the inspection and verification processes, both the customer and the delivery agent can proceed with the final handover of the vehicle, ensuring a smooth delivery experience for the customer.</p></div>
